<%/* Fix it on a branch, asked first in the modal: until now the agent has
     only read the project. Making the branch lets it change files there, so
     it says what happens and where before it does. The conversation carries
     on as the fix's, its sessions moved into the fix's folder on the
     branch. The name is asked here, once a branch needs one, starting from
     the conversation's own. Refused, the fields come back alone. `it` is
     the conversation (a fix with no branch); `it.$fields` the fields as
     refused, on a cold load. */%>
<% const base = `/f/${it.folder.id}/d/${it.id}`; %>
<div class="stack gap-4" ko-item>
  <h2>Fix it on a branch</h2>
  <div class="notice">
    <p>Prelude makes a branch for this fix from main, in a worktree of its own, and the agent fixes it there: in the app, the designs or both, keeping the designs in step. Each turn is committed to the branch. Nothing reaches main until you merge it, or push it for a pull request.</p>
    <p>This conversation carries on as the fix’s, and moves into the project with it.</p>
  </div>
  <form class="stack" action="<%= base %>/branch" method="post" ko-target="fields">
    <div ko-as="fields"><%~ include('./_fix-branch-fields', it.$fields ?? { title: it.title }) %></div>
    <%/* The preview's: the branch it would make, as the app's model has it
         after. The app works these out itself and reads only the title. */%>
    <input type="hidden" name="branch.id" value="<%= it.id.replace('fixes/', 'fix-') %>">
    <input type="hidden" name="branch.branch" value="prelude/<%= it.id.replace('fixes/', 'fix-') %>">
    <input type="hidden" name="branch.into" value="main">
    <div class="cluster actions">
      <button class="btn primary" type="submit"><span class="icon icon-push" aria-hidden="true"></span>Make the branch and fix it</button>
      <button class="btn ghost" type="button" command="--koda-empty" commandfor="modal">Not now</button>
    </div>
  </form>
</div>
